WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:08.080
David, given the fiasco with Trump not conceding,&nbsp;
should presidential transitions really depend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:14.080
on an administration official of the sitting&nbsp;
president like Emily Murphy at the GSA? This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:20.160
a great question. The framework for the official&nbsp;
transition is outlined by the Presidential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:30.000
Transition Act of 1963. And insofar as that&nbsp;
outlines the official piece of the transition the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.240
General Service Administration had, Emily Murphy&nbsp;
was the person who had to authorize about seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.760
million dollars in funds to be made available&nbsp;
to Joe Biden to officially start the transition.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:51.200
Now, in a sense, the transition doesn't really&nbsp;
depend on her. And what I mean by that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:59.680
the GSA had, as directed by Trump, doesn't really&nbsp;
need to do anything in order for Joe Biden to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:05.840
president and sworn in on January 20th. These&nbsp;
are separate processes. What the GSA process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:13.200
does is it recognizes the current administration&nbsp;
sees the president elect as the president elect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:18.080
We are freeing up funding. It greases the wheels&nbsp;
for starting to give Joe Biden the presidential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:24.000
daily briefing and facilitating some other&nbsp;
things. But either way, on January 20th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.960
Trump stops being president and the Supreme Court&nbsp;
chief justice swears in the new president. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:38.640
doesn't actually depend on the GSA. That being&nbsp;
said, I do believe that at this point in time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:45.520
listen, the explanation that Emily Murphy gave&nbsp;
was I'm supposed to ascertain the winner of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:51.760
election. I'm not supposed to impose the winner&nbsp;
on the country. And because it was contested.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:58.480
It was not totally clear to me that I could&nbsp;
ascertain the winner yet, but now I have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.240
and she's tried to kind of pull herself out of&nbsp;
this as a partizan actor. It's basically B.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:11.520
historically, with the exception of the year&nbsp;
2000, where it really did depend on one recount&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:17.600
in one state and it took about a month for that&nbsp;
to be formally recognized. It's pretty clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:24.000
that there has been an apparent winner and there&nbsp;
was no reason whatsoever that Emily Murphy should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.320
not have done this earlier. And in the 21st&nbsp;
century, you know, at this point in time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.080
the longest it should really take to ascertain the&nbsp;
winner of an election is a few days. And that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.800
what it took. Within a few days, it was clear that&nbsp;
Joe Biden was going to be the next president. So I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:44.880
do think it would be I mean, listen, this is&nbsp;
a reminder of what this reminds us, that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:50.800
have certain checks and balances in this country&nbsp;
that work OK, as long as you don't have anybody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:57.440
violating the obvious norms. And Donald Trump,&nbsp;
if he did anything, is he went against all of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:03.840
norms, you know, Hatch Act sharing classified&nbsp;
information, all of these different things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:12.240
So what we've learned is you could have someone as&nbsp;
whacked as Trump that doesn't abide by the norms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.400
And then you can have a situation where&nbsp;
Emily Murphy spends almost a month&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.800
before formally authorizing the transition. It's&nbsp;
sort of a microcosm of the Trump presidency.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.720
We probably should have some more concrete&nbsp;
requirements for the GSA right now. Again, it says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.320
the GSA should ascertain the winner&nbsp;
of the election. It doesn't say how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.680
typically, you know, the media calls the race and&nbsp;
that's not official. It's not official until the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:41.120
electors actually vote. But the GSA goes with&nbsp;
it and the process begins. But there's nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.000
in the law that explicitly says that that's&nbsp;
how it has to happen. So I would like to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.680
something made more explicit. Again, it wouldn't&nbsp;
have prevented Biden from becoming president.&nbsp;

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:56.720
He would have anyway. But she certainly was&nbsp;
able to gum up elements of the transition and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:02.480
you could spell it out much more specifically.&nbsp;
That's my thought. The important point is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:07.280
transition doesn't actually depend on the&nbsp;
current administration. They certainly can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:12.400
get in the way of some funding for the transition.&nbsp;
But ultimately, the presidency would end and Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:18.000
Biden would become president regardless on January&nbsp;
20th. We've got a great bonus show for you today.&nbsp;

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:25.120
Get instant access to the bonus show by&nbsp;
becoming a member at joint Pakman Dotcom.

